      "[PART 1 HAS BEEN COMPLETE WE ARE WORKING ON PART 2 NOW]\n\n**Part 1 / Document 1 Sections:**\nMaintain few technical details, introduced the reader to the concepts. \n\n[PART 1 HAS BEEN COMPLETE WE ARE WORKING ON PART 2 NOW]\n \n [Title]\n [TOC]\n [Capability Claims]\n  - List all the capabilities , no explanation, frame it as a list of AI Super Powers\n [Verification Templates]\n  - Prompt templates to verify claims. \n [Architecture Summary Overview]\n - A brief summary of the legacy 104 era and the current 105 era. A short and sweet introduction to the versions, each of their 3 format versions and the MFDB architecture that sits on top, define it as an orchistration layer of the formats  not a format itself. Should be concise with few technical details.\n [Positional Access Field Seperation]\n  - A brief explanation of the fields, how they are separated from the values, define the terms (fields, values  records as rows which hold sets of values). Define Record Types, 104 and 104a being single typed and 104db being multi typed but meant for small data sets, Clarify that it is not MFDB, . Clarify that the purpose of all of this is for AI readability, token,memory and context optimizations. Detail that MFDB orchistrates the formats to managing them as a relational database that enforces cascade referential integrity. Maintain few technical terms in this section , just define things and briefly explain each\n  \n\n\n[PART 1 HAS BEEN COMPLETE WE ARE WORKING ON PART 2 NOW]\n\n[START HERE]\n\n  **Part 2 / Document 2 Sections**\n [BEJSON] \n \nDetailed subsections of each of the 3 formats. Explain the universal rules and format specific rules, the purpose of the format, its suggested use cases. DO NOT DETAIL EVERY VALIDATION RULE THIS IS NOT THE PLACE, JUST DEFINE ITS STRUCTURE... PROVIDE SCHDMA EXAMPLES.\n [MFDB]\nExplain MFDB, how it orchistrates 104 and 104a files, the bi directial integrity, the Network master and slave roles the context window benefits, the way it accesses only what it needs. It's usage of _fk, manifest cordination. DO NOT DETAIL EVERY VALIDATION RULE THIS IS NOT THE PLACE, JUST DEFINE ITS STRUCTURE... PROVIDE SCHDMA EXAMPLES. \n [Field Map Cache]\n Explain what index based lookups are, why they fail and our solution.\n [UUID Addressing] \n Explain how we do not reference by field name or row/col position but by Zuuid and why \n [Crash Course Rules]\n Here we define every validation rule.",
      "Author a comprehensive 4-part technical publication on: [PART 1 HAS BEEN COMPLETE WE ARE WORKING ON PART 2 NOW]\n\n**Part 1 / Document 1 Sections:**\nMaintain few technical details, introduced the reader to the concepts. \n\n[PART 1 HAS BEEN COMPLETE WE ARE WORKING ON PART 2 NOW]\n \n [Title]\n [TOC]\n [Capability Claims]\n  - List all the capabilities , no explanation, frame it as a list of AI Super Powers\n [Verification Templates]\n  - Prompt templates to verify claims. \n [Architecture Summary Overview]\n - A brief summary of the legacy 104 era and the current 105 era. A short and sweet introduction to the versions, each of their 3 format versions and the MFDB architecture that sits on top, define it as an orchistration layer of the formats  not a format itself. Should be concise with few technical details.\n [Positional Access Field Seperation]\n  - A brief explanation of the fields, how they are separated from the values, define the terms (fields, values  records as rows which hold sets of values). Define Record Types, 104 and 104a being single typed and 104db being multi typed but meant for small data sets, Clarify that it is not MFDB, . Clarify that the purpose of all of this is for AI readability, token,memory and context optimizations. Detail that MFDB orchistrates the formats to managing them as a relational database that enforces cascade referential integrity. Maintain few technical terms in this section , just define things and briefly explain each\n  \n\n\n[PART 1 HAS BEEN COMPLETE WE ARE WORKING ON PART 2 NOW]\n\n[START HERE]\n\n  **Part 2 / Document 2 Sections**\n [BEJSON] \n \nDetailed subsections of each of the 3 formats. Explain the universal rules and format specific rules, the purpose of the format, its suggested use cases. DO NOT DETAIL EVERY VALIDATION RULE THIS IS NOT THE PLACE, JUST DEFINE ITS STRUCTURE... PROVIDE SCHDMA EXAMPLES.\n [MFDB]\nExplain MFDB, how it orchistrates 104 and 104a files, the bi directial integrity, the Network master and slave roles the context window benefits, the way it accesses only what it needs. It's usage of _fk, manifest cordination. DO NOT DETAIL EVERY VALIDATION RULE THIS IS NOT THE PLACE, JUST DEFINE ITS STRUCTURE... PROVIDE SCHDMA EXAMPLES. \n [Field Map Cache]\n Explain what index based lookups are, why they fail and our solution.\n [UUID Addressing] \n Explain how we do not reference by field name or row/col position but by Zuuid and why \n [Crash Course Rules]\n Here we define every validation rule.",
